\item{\code{combined}}{float; in \strong{fraction of discoveries (an FDP estimate; can exceed 1)}; never \code{NA}. Eq. 1, N_E (1 + 1/r) / (N_T + N_E). An upper bound: at or below the claimed FDR, it is evidence of control. Not capped at 1.}
\item{\code{paired}}{float; in \strong{fraction of discoveries (an FDP estimate; can exceed 1)}; \code{NA} when does not apply: the ratio is not exactly 1, or every entrapment is foreign. Eq. 4, (N_E + N_\{E>=s>T\} + 2 N_\{E>T>=s\}) / (N_T + N_E): a tighter upper bound for 1:1 pairing. N_\{E>=s>T\} counts discovered entrapments whose partner was not discovered (no partner counts so); N_\{E>T>=s\} those whose partner was discovered but ranked behind them, by lower q-value and then higher score, an exact tie counting the entrapment ahead. Not capped at 1.}
