\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item Wen et al. 2025, as FDRBench implements it. lower_bound can only show that a search fails to control its FDR; combined is an upper bound, evidence that it does; paired is a tighter upper bound for 1:1 pairing. None is capped at 1.
\item A candidate is discovered when its q-value is at or below the threshold, and a partner by its own q-value. A discovered pair is ranked lower q-value first, then higher score, and an exact tie counts against the search.
\item Give one row per unit estimated (precursor, peptide or protein group), decoys removed, each with its best q-value: mzLib does not deduplicate. A partner's score and q-value are copies of its target's row, and mzLib does not check them.
\item paired is reported only for a ratio of exactly 1 with some entrapment not foreign. The sample estimator N_E / (r N_T), invalid in both directions, is deliberately absent (mzLib), and the k-fold paired estimator for k entrapments per target is not implemented.
\item An entrapment generator's exclusions change the inputs in opposite directions (mzLib's EntrapmentFdp.ClassifyExclusion): an entrapment that is really a target peptide comes out of the entrapments file; a target that cannot be traced to one target stays in the targets file but is nobody's partner.
}
}
